# Lower bound for dim M_k(Γ₁(M)), k≥ 3, M≥ 5

Theorem statement: `ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card`
(`e52e7754-dd59-54dc-8282-e638ce354cfe`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `938c3173-ee4f-5f3a-bbcb-7e51cd60b0e7`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$, and let $k$ be a natural number with $3 \le k$.
The assertion is that there exist a natural number $d$ and a family $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to
M_k(\Gamma_1(M))$ of modular forms of weight $k$ (the integer $k$) for the congruence subgroup
$\Gamma_1(M) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ which is linearly independent over $\mathbb{C}$ and
satisfies the numerical inequality
$$(k-1)\,[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(M)\cdot\{\pm 1\}] + 6\,c \;\le\; 12\,d,$$
where the index is that of the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$
together with $-1$ (the join of $\Gamma_1(M)$ with the cyclic group of integral powers of $-1$), and
$c$ is the cardinality of the set of double cosets $\Gamma_1(M)\backslash
\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\langle T, -1\rangle$, the subgroup on the right being generated by the
translation matrix $T$ and by $-1$. All arithmetic is in $\mathbb{N}$, so $k-1$ is truncated
subtraction; since $k \ge 3$ this is the ordinary difference. Since the forms are linearly
independent, the conclusion is a lower bound for $\dim_{\mathbb{C}} M_k(\Gamma_1(M))$ and not an
exact dimension formula.

This is the existence half of the classical dimension formula for $M_k(\Gamma_1(M))$ in the range $k
\ge 3$, $M \ge 5$, where $\Gamma_1(M)$ has no elliptic points, does not contain $-1$ and has only
regular cusps; in that range $12\dim_{\mathbb{C}} M_k(\Gamma_1(M)) =
(k-1)[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma_1(M)] + 6c$, the double-coset count $c$ being the number
of cusps of $\Gamma_1(M)$, and the statement records the inequality $\le$ in the form needed later.
It feeds
[`ModularCurve.exists_isIntegralQExp_linearIndependent_complex_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_isIntegralQExp_linearIndependent_complex_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card),
which refines the independent family to one with integral $q$-expansions.

